WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.279
Ramanujan is an inspirational figure. After
all, he’s the topic of a popular Hollywood

00:00:06.279 --> 00:00:10.870
film now, The Man Who Knew Infinity. But he’s
much more than an inspirational figure to

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:17.050
me. He’s been a guardian angel to me. And
as impossible as that might sound, to believe,

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:24.439
I have to tell you he was — the news of
Ramanujan was very important to me as a 16-year

00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:29.720
old. As a 16-year-old high-schooler I was
trained that — I was trained to believe

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:35.030
that to be successful you had to be a perfect,
straight-A student. You had to get perfect

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:41.940
test scores. Of course they’re important,
but Mrs. Ramanujan wrote a letter to my father

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:49.039
in 1984 when I was in 10th grade over 60 years
after Ramanujan died. And that’s I when first

00:00:49.039 --> 00:00:54.059
learned about this great genius who was not
well known for grades. If anything he was

00:00:54.059 --> 00:00:59.460
well known for being a two-time college dropout,
but a real artist, a genius, someone who’s

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:05.810
mathematical ideas were pure flights of fancy.
I learned about him again in college when

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:12.220
the NOVA special about him came out. And Professor
Paul Sally, one of my most important mentors

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:18.820
in my life, came along and we talked about
Ramanujan and the importance of his ideas.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:23.610
And then of course in graduate when the book
The Man Who Knew Infinity came out, together

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:29.670
with my adviser Basil Gordon, we read it and
we got a lot of strength out of it. At least

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:36.549
certainly I did. And certainly at those three
points in my life — as a high school student,

00:01:36.549 --> 00:01:41.049
and a college student and later as a graduate
student — I needed to be reminded and reassured

00:01:41.049 --> 00:01:48.520
that the time was going to come that I would
be evaluated professionally for my achievement

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:56.030
and not test scores and not grades. And in
that way I think he’s been my guardian angel

00:01:56.030 --> 00:02:00.649
and you know in my work I’ve been following
him professionally and it’s worked out very

00:02:00.649 --> 00:02:01.170
well for me.

